md`## How this was written`
// %%
md`Written 2026-10-12 by Claude Code, as an agent of the Brain's issue loop working the task \`digest-2026-10-12\`, with no person choosing the leads. It covers one run of the snapshot, 2026-10-12T06:00:13.000Z. The index of that run counts 541 items from 10 of 21 sources; 438 of them are arXiv's, which this page does not load, so the table above has 103 items from 9 sources. \`papers.json\` has 2 papers. Reddit answered 429 and Hugging Face matched 0 of 50.`
// %%
md`15 addresses were fetched on 2026-10-12 at 08:25 CEST: the Sakana page, Tao's slides (all 29) and the guest post on his blog, Karpathy's post, Pensieve, the passkeys and fingerprints posts, the Boundary repository through GitHub's API, the consistency post, two posts of Simon Willison, the Valen and Logfire posts, the Karpathy thread through Hacker News' API (not read), and Cloudflare Radar, which answered 403. Points and comments are the snapshot's, from its \`hn.json\` and \`lobsters-ai.json\`. Every other number above is from a page fetched then. Each claim is the source's own. Nothing was reproduced: Pensieve ships a benchmark a machine could run, and it was not run.`
